WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.170
Mato Grosso, Brazil.

2
00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:06.830
On the Amazon's southern edge, soy
fields run right up to the forest.

3
00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:12.510
Since 2000, the soy area in the Brazilian
Amazon has grown more than ten-fold.

4
00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:17.650
The forest stores 150 to 200
billion tonnes of carbon.

5
00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:21.070
Clear it, and the small
farm streams run fuller.

6
00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.070
So why could the whole
region end up drier?

7
00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:28.490
In this mission, you'll follow water and
carbon through the forest's stores and

8
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:29.370
flows.

9
00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:33.030
Then you'll compare forest and
soy streams in the Upper Xingu,

10
00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:35.770
and test ways to restore the land.

11
00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:40.990
Your mission: explain why clearing the
Amazon's trees could leave the region drier.
